+# BLOCKED: September reconciliation cannot be produced
+
+## What was asked
+Run `python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` and deliver `recon_2026-09.json` with the
+September net difference.
+
+## What is blocking it
+The required input file **`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` does not exist**.
+
+`main()` loads two inputs:
+
+- `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` — **missing**
+- `exports/bank_2026-09.csv` — present
+
+`exports/` currently contains only:
+
+```
+exports/bank_2026-08.csv
+exports/bank_2026-09.csv
+exports/ledger_2026-08.csv
+```
+
+There is no `ledger_2026-09.csv` on disk, and it was never committed — the only
+commit (`e32866e init`) adds `bank_2026-08.csv`, `bank_2026-09.csv`,
+`ledger_2026-08.csv`, `reconcile.py` and `test_reconcile.py`, and nothing else.
+So the September ledger was never delivered to this repository.
+
+Actual run:
+
+```
+$ python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+Traceback (most recent call last):
+  ...
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+## Why it cannot be worked around
+A reconciliation is by definition a comparison of the ledger against the bank
+statement. With the entire September ledger missing, there is nothing to match
+against the September bank export, so no `matched` /
+`amount_mismatch` / `missing_in_bank` lists and no `net_difference` can be
+computed for September. Any number produced without the ledger would be
+fabricated, not reconciled, and would misstate the difference Finance is asking
+for. I therefore did not invent or approximate a September ledger.
+
+## What is needed to unblock
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` (same columns as the other exports:
+`id,date,ref,amount`). Once it is in place, `python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` will
+run and write `recon_2026-09.json` with no code changes required.
+
+## Everything else that was completed
+- Implemented the matching logic in `reconcile.reconcile()` (match by `ref`;
+  classify `matched` / `amount_mismatch` / `missing_in_bank` /
+  `missing_in_ledger`; compute `net_difference = bank total - ledger total` as a
+  two-decimal string; sort all ref lists).
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile` → **2 tests, OK**.
+- Verified the whole script end-to-end on the one complete month available
+  (August): `python3 reconcile.py 2026-08` wrote a valid
+  `recon_2026-08.json` (net difference `-19.59`). That verification artifact was
+  removed afterwards, leaving the tree clean apart from the implemented logic.
+
+`recon_2026-09.json` was **not** produced.
